IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei1-payment`
IMPORT `ei1-benefit-period`
IMPORT `ei1-parental`

-- Tests of ei1-parental.l4 (Act s 23). Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named
-- beside the assertion; none is copied from the module's output. Dates were worked out with a calendar program that is
-- not the encoding. One #ASSERT per line.

§ `s 23(1) who may claim parental benefits (src:509)`
-- args: major attachment claimant; to care for a new-born child of the claimant; to care for a child placed for adoption under the law of the province of residence
#ASSERT `s 23(1) benefits are payable to the claimant to care for one or more new-born or adopted children` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(1) benefits are payable to the claimant to care for one or more new-born or adopted children` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(1) benefits are payable to the claimant to care for one or more new-born or adopted children` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(1) benefits are payable to the claimant to care for one or more new-born or adopted children` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 23(1.1) to (1.3) the election (src:511-515)`
#ASSERT `s 23(1.1) the maximum number of weeks elected` `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `s 23(1.1) the maximum number of weeks elected` `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 61
#ASSERT `s 23(1.2) the election is irrevocable` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(1.2) the election is irrevocable` FALSE)
-- args: the claimant's own election; the election of the first to claim in respect of the same child or children, if another has claimed
#ASSERT `s 23(1.3) the election that binds the claimant` `the 35-week maximum` NOTHING EQUALS `the 35-week maximum`
#ASSERT `s 23(1.3) the election that binds the claimant` `the 61-week maximum` NOTHING EQUALS `the 61-week maximum`
#ASSERT `s 23(1.3) the election that binds the claimant` `the 35-week maximum` (JUST `the 61-week maximum`) EQUALS `the 61-week maximum`
#ASSERT `s 23(1.3) the election that binds the claimant` `the 61-week maximum` (JUST `the 35-week maximum`) EQUALS `the 35-week maximum`

§ `s 23(2) the period during which benefits are payable (src:517-519)`
-- A child born on Wednesday 2026-03-04 (the week of Sunday 2026-03-01): the period runs from 2026-03-01 to Saturday 2027-03-06, the last day of the week 52 weeks after.
#ASSERT (`s 23(2) the period during which benefits are payable` (YMD 2026 3 4))'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT (`s 23(2) the period during which benefits are payable` (YMD 2026 3 4))'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 6
#ASSERT (`s 23(2) the period during which benefits are payable` (YMD 2026 3 1))'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT (`s 23(2) the period during which benefits are payable` (YMD 2026 3 7))'s `first day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT (`s 23(2) the period during which benefits are payable` (YMD 2026 3 7))'s `last day of the period` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 6

§ `s 23(3), s 23(3.01) and s 23(3.1) hospital and Canadian Forces weeks (src:521-525)`
#ASSERT `s 23(3) the number of weeks by which the period is extended because the children are in hospital` TRUE 5 EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `s 23(3) the number of weeks by which the period is extended because the children are in hospital` FALSE 5 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 23(3.01) the number of weeks by which the period is extended because of the Canadian Forces` TRUE 7 EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `s 23(3.01) the number of weeks by which the period is extended because of the Canadian Forces` FALSE 7 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 23(3.1) the longest the period may be after an extension under subsection (3) or (3.01), in weeks` EQUALS 104

§ `s 23(3.2) the conditions and the extension (src:527-531)`
`ei1 test parental pregnancy 15` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `pregnancy`, 15
`ei1 test parental parental 40` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `caring for a new-born or adopted child`, 40
`ei1 test parental parental 61` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `caring for a new-born or adopted child`, 61
`ei1 test parental parental 20` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `caring for a new-born or adopted child`, 20
`ei1 test parental sickness 20` MEANS `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`, 20
-- args: regular benefits were paid; the special benefits paid; the election
-- 15 + 61 = 76 is more than 50; parental benefits were paid for 40 of 61 weeks: yes
#ASSERT `s 23(3.2) the period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test parental pregnancy 15`, `ei1 test parental parental 40`) `the 61-week maximum`
-- the parental benefits were paid for the full 61 weeks: (d) fails
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(3.2) the period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test parental pregnancy 15`, `ei1 test parental parental 61`) `the 61-week maximum`)
-- no parental benefits among two reasons: (d) fails
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(3.2) the period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test parental pregnancy 15`, `ei1 test parental sickness 20`) `the 61-week maximum`)
-- regular benefits were paid
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(3.2) the period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks` TRUE (LIST `ei1 test parental pregnancy 15`, `ei1 test parental parental 40`) `the 61-week maximum`)
-- one reason only
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(3.2) the period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test parental parental 40`) `the 61-week maximum`)
-- 15 + 35 = 50 is not more than 50
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(3.2) the period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test parental pregnancy 15`, `ei1 test parental parental 20`) `the 35-week maximum`)
-- the extension: the length of s 10(15), 2 + 76 = 78, less 52 weeks
#ASSERT `s 23(3.2) the number of weeks by which the period is extended` TRUE (LIST `ei1 test parental pregnancy 15`, `ei1 test parental parental 40`) `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `s 23(3.2) the number of weeks by which the period is extended` FALSE (LIST `ei1 test parental pregnancy 15`, `ei1 test parental parental 40`) `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 0

§ `s 23(3.21) an extension of 26 weeks for the 61-week election (src:533-536)`
-- args: benefits were paid for the 12(3)(b) reason; the election; regular benefits were paid; benefits were paid for another special reason
#ASSERT `s 23(3.21) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` TRUE `the 61-week maximum` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `s 23(3.21) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` TRUE `the 35-week maximum` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 23(3.21) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` TRUE `the 61-week maximum` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 23(3.21) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` TRUE `the 61-week maximum` FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 23(3.21) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` FALSE `the 61-week maximum` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0

§ `s 23(3.22) regular and special benefits (src:538)`
-- args: regular benefits were paid; benefits for the 12(3)(b) reason; the election; fewer than the total weeks; the extension established under s 10(13.02)
#ASSERT `s 23(3.22) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for regular and special benefits` TRUE TRUE `the 61-week maximum` TRUE 12 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `s 23(3.22) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for regular and special benefits` FALSE TRUE `the 61-week maximum` TRUE 12 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 23(3.22) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for regular and special benefits` TRUE FALSE `the 61-week maximum` TRUE 12 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 23(3.22) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for regular and special benefits` TRUE TRUE `the 35-week maximum` TRUE 12 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 23(3.22) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for regular and special benefits` TRUE TRUE `the 61-week maximum` FALSE 12 EQUALS 0

§ `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks (src:521-543)`
-- args: weeks under (3), (3.01), (3.2), (3.21), (3.22); the maximum number of weeks of s 10(15)
#ASSERT `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks` 0 0 0 0 0 78 EQUALS 52
#ASSERT `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks` 4 0 0 0 0 78 EQUALS 56
#ASSERT `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks` 60 0 0 0 0 78 EQUALS 104
#ASSERT `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks` 30 30 0 0 0 78 EQUALS 104
#ASSERT `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks` 0 0 26 0 0 78 EQUALS 78
#ASSERT `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks` 0 0 26 0 0 70 EQUALS 70
#ASSERT `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks` 30 0 26 0 0 78 EQUALS 82
#ASSERT `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks` 0 0 0 26 0 52 EQUALS 78
#ASSERT `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks` 0 0 0 0 10 52 EQUALS 62
#ASSERT `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks` 4 0 26 26 10 78 EQUALS 104

§ `s 23(3.5) a provincial law allowance reduces the benefits (src:545)`
#ASSERT `s 23(3.5) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` TRUE TRUE 400 150 EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `s 23(3.5) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` TRUE TRUE 400 500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 23(3.5) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` TRUE FALSE 400 150 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `s 23(3.5) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` FALSE TRUE 400 150 EQUALS 400

§ `s 23(4), (4.1) and (4.11) dividing the weeks (src:547-553)`
#ASSERT `s 23(4) and s 23(4.1) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants` `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `s 23(4) and s 23(4.1) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants` `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 69
#ASSERT `s 23(4.11) the most weeks of benefits that may be paid to one claimant` `the 35-week maximum` EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `s 23(4.11) the most weeks of benefits that may be paid to one claimant` `the 61-week maximum` EQUALS 61
-- args: the election; weeks divided to the first claimant; weeks divided to the second
#ASSERT `s 23(4) the division of the weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limits` `the 35-week maximum` 20 20
#ASSERT `s 23(4) the division of the weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limits` `the 35-week maximum` 35 5
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(4) the division of the weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limits` `the 35-week maximum` 36 4)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(4) the division of the weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limits` `the 35-week maximum` 21 20)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(4) the division of the weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limits` `the 35-week maximum` 35 35)
#ASSERT `s 23(4) the division of the weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limits` `the 61-week maximum` 61 8
#ASSERT `s 23(4) the division of the weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limits` `the 61-week maximum` 35 34
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(4) the division of the weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limits` `the 61-week maximum` 62 7)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(4) the division of the weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limits` `the 61-week maximum` 35 35)
#ASSERT `s 23(4) the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with the prescribed rules` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(4) the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with the prescribed rules` TRUE)

§ `s 23(5) deferring the waiting period (src:555-559)`
-- args: a major attachment claimant who claims under section 23; (a) already claimed and served; (b) another has claimed and served or is serving; (c) another is claiming at the same time and elects to serve; (d) prescribed requirements
#ASSERT `s 23(5) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(5) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(5) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 23(5) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(5) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 23(5) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `s 23(6) a major attachment claimant and an individual claim for the same child (src:561-563)`
-- args: both claims are made; one of them has served or elected to serve the waiting period; it is the major attachment claimant who did
#ASSERT `s 23(6) the position of the waiting period when a major attachment claimant and an individual claim for the same child` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `ei1 the major attachment claimant is not required to serve a waiting period`
#ASSERT `s 23(6) the position of the waiting period when a major attachment claimant and an individual claim for the same child` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ei1 the individual may have their waiting period deferred in accordance with section 152.05`
#ASSERT `s 23(6) the position of the waiting period when a major attachment claimant and an individual claim for the same child` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `ei1 subsection 23(6) does not apply`
#ASSERT `s 23(6) the position of the waiting period when a major attachment claimant and an individual claim for the same child` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `ei1 subsection 23(6) does not apply`
